<i>Yeah, come on!</i>

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:51.120
Chapter 15 Poetry

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:19.180
Are you that worried?

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:24.080
Mr. Okita!

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:27.870
Please don't whisper into
my ear! Not into my ear!

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:31.420
So, it's doing things by your
ear that's your weakness.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:34.000
No, that's not the issue here!

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:37.250
I'm only kidding.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:40.240
You were thinking about Tetsu, weren't you?

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:43.420
Well, yes.

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:50.750
But I think you can stop worrying now.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:55.000
It seems Tetsu has completely
returned to being his old self.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.610
I hope that's the case.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:03.120
Oh? You almost sound as if you
don't want Tetsu to cheer up.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.660
Oh, that's...

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:08.000
not true, is it? Naturally.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.440
Of course not!

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:20.040
You do not need anyone interfering in matters
between you and your brother, was it?

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.790
Oh, no, I am so sorry!

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:25.850
Back then, I was just so frantic...

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:32.100
Oh!

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.380
I just had a great idea!

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:41.370
What?!

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:58.380
Where is it?! Where did it go?!

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:04.010
It had better not...

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:13.600
It had better not...!

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:16.770
You got any other dirty
laundry or anything?

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.250
Yeah, I left it out there.

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:20.750
Got it!

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:24.110
What's this, Ichimura?
You're awfully enthusiastic today.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:27.790
Well, I wasted a couple
of days there, so...

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:31.290
Hey, that's real commendable
of you to say that.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:33.870
Well, don't push yourself too hard.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:34.750
Right!

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:41.330
Oh, Mr. Okita?

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:43.510
What are you looking all happy about?

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:46.010
It's this thing here.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.510
Hougyoku Haiku Collection

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:48.510
It's a collection of haiku,

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:52.080
But it's just an absolute riot!

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:55.450
Haiku? By whom?

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:56.690
It's a secret.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:58.760
Oh, I know! It's yours!

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:03.610
Sorry, wrong!

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:08.500
Come on! Please tell me!
I really want to know now!

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:12.040
At least one haiku! It's okay if
I just take a peek inside, right?!

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:15.410
Please?!
Oh, all right.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:17.790
I'll make an exception just for you.

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:20.250
The truth is,

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:24.080
this is an encryption of the
Shinsengumi's top-secret information.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:28.830
Be wary not to accidentally
let it leak to any outsiders.

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:30.560
Or your head will roll.

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:50.620
But I am only joking.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:54.330
Oh? You look as if you're about
to wet yourself any minute now.

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:04.190
"Hougyoku Haiku Collection"?

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:07.420
Who's Hougyoku?

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:10.870
Never mind that. Hurry up and look inside.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:12.000
Okay.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.790
How about this one?

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:17.430
"In a rundown shack, lying there it
is most cold, I see the spring moon."

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:23.650
Well, if you're sleeping in a shack,
of course it'll be cold!

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:27.660
This one's incredible too!

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:29.410
Let's see...

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:33.330
"A bush warbler cries, I hear and
stop my dusting, all unwittingly."

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:35.710
He must have been in the
middle of cleaning.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:39.790
Talking about dusting
is just weird somehow!

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:43.960
"Apricot flower, though you
have one bloom, you are..."

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:46.300
"an apricot still."

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:49.340
"The seven spring herbs,
up to five of them have I..."

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:53.370
"put to memory."

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:58.660
This guy's memory is terrible!

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:00.310
It really is, isn't it?

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:04.830
Every single haiku is absolutely hilarious!

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:08.000
So whose is it anyway?

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.950
That would be...

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:10.990
That would be?

00:07:22.910 --> 00:07:24.200
Was that...?

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.080
Tetsu, here, you can have it.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:28.260
What? Wait!

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:32.810
Soji!

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:39.130
Damn.

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:45.850
So he got away.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:49.750
Mr. Hijikata...

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:52.610
Did he read it to you?

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:54.450
The haiku!

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:58.480
Well...

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:02.620
Which means Hougyoku,
who wrote that collection of haiku, is...

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:05.200
Soji, come on out!

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:09.380
Give back my collection
of haiku right this minute!

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:14.760
Well, I have my page duties to
attend to, so please excuse me.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.090
Ichimura...

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:21.230
The way you're walking
is strangely peculiar.

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:23.730
You think so?

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:28.700
It's as if you have something
hidden in your shirt.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:32.860
Let's see...

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:37.950
the contents!

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:42.200
Tetsu, run!

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:43.790
Mr. Okita!

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:46.830
Damn it, Soji! Let me go!

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:51.130
I'll hold off Mr. Hijikata!

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:56.130
Tetsu, you take that collection of haiku
and run to the ends of the Earth!

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:58.950
Let go, Soji!

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:00.120
Mr. Okita...

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:01.660
Hurry!

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:06.730
Restrain yourself!

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:09.330
<i>Mr. Okita, I'm sorry.</i>

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:12.000
<i>But I... But I...</i>

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:16.160
<i>I won't fail you! Just watch,
I'll take this collection and escape!</i>

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:18.620
<i>Yes, all the way to the ends of the Earth!</i>

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:19.280
<i>Tetsu</i>...

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:21.700
Take this! And this!

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:26.500
Hold it, Ichimura!

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:30.630
After a hundred lashes to your bottom,

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:33.130
you're going without dinner!

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:35.540
Oh, come on!

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:39.980
It's noisy here.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:48.250
I am truly very sorry, Master.

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:53.700
However, they have been notified to avoid
going out during the day as much as possible,

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:57.030
so we cannot deprive them
of this sort of thing...

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:00.910
Hey, we're running low on sake here!

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:03.160
Aren't there any snacks
to go with the drinks?!

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:06.160
Hurry it up!

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:07.960
A true loyalist...

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:14.120
keeps his madness sheathed in reason.

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:18.830
Hotaru, was that you again?!

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:20.540
I'm so sorry!

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:23.250
The people on the second floor
want everything so fast!

00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:26.450
That's enough! Hurry and clean it up!

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:28.060
Yes, sir!

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:30.950
Master?

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:35.200
It is too noisy here.
We're going out, Suzu.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:35.840
Yes, sir.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:39.320
I need to speak with you.

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:51.880
Isn't that the hairdresser who's
been coming and going lately?

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:57.000
Is something wrong, Master?

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.050
No.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:04.120
Wait, now that I think about it,

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:08.060
why do I have to be running
away with this stupid thing?

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:10.950
How dare you call it "this stupid thing"?!

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:14.520
Hurry up and give it back!

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:19.620
Has Mr. Hijikata gone insane?

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:22.290
What's this? Toshi in a headlong sprint?

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:24.490
I haven't seen that in a while.

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:28.160
Stop him, sheesh.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:35.540
Ichimura!

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:39.010
You won't get away with this!

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:40.840
Help!

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:51.180
<i>Who the hell is this?</i>

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:55.290
It's dangerous, ya know!

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:00.690
He's gone.

00:12:27.910 --> 00:12:32.000
Looks like I got away somehow,
thanks to that guy.

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:37.200
But Mr. Okita's so mean,
making me take this thing.

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:38.610
Hey!

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:42.700
What're you doing out here, puppy boy?

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:45.490
Get chewed out by Mr. Hijikata again?

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:49.290
Anyway, get a load of this!

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:53.500
We got some fresh vegetables
from a nearby farm!

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:57.290
Never mind any of that! Here!

00:12:58.160 --> 00:12:59.710
What's this?

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:08.500
Are these good or bad?
They're so nonsensical, I can't tell!

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:12.200
"though you have one bloom..."?
Well, of course it is!

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:20.320
Tetsu, would you tell me the
meaning hidden in these haiku?

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:23.150
Well, I didn't compose those haiku.

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:26.540
Sorry about that. I shouldn't
have laughed at them.

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:30.580
I know, I bet these have some
deep meaning to them, right?

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:32.240
I'm telling you...

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:35.120
Hey, this one's got an odd touch to it too!

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:36.950
Yeah? Lemme see.

00:13:36.950 --> 00:13:40.870
"Field mustards beyond, upon that
reed screen rises, oh, the morning sun."

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:43.700
Whoa! Mystery!
Mystery!

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:49.330
Sorry, guess we've been
laughing a bit too hard.

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:53.520
We got too serious over haiku a
15-year-old composed for practice.

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:57.120
Okay, so tell us what these haiku mean.

00:13:57.120 --> 00:14:00.370
Then we'll be able to give you
more of a proper critique.

00:14:00.370 --> 00:14:02.290
That's right.

00:14:06.410 --> 00:14:07.900
So you want to hear?

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:13.330
What those haiku mean...

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:16.620
You're saying you want to hear?

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:19.400
This collection of haiku...

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:21.670
Don't tell me...

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:25.340
I'm asking you if you want to hear!

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:28.620
What's going on?!

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:30.000
Hell if I know!

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.000
This is Mr. Hijikata's collection of haiku!

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:34.000
What?!

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:36.540
Say that sooner!

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:40.520
You bastards, hold it right there!

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:43.020
He's damn scary!

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:46.360
The vegetables!

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:58.330
Oh, we did it.

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:01.950
Thinking about what'll happen
later is even more scary, but...

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:03.380
Now's our chance!

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:05.710
Run away!

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:14.260
By a mere potato...

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:17.540
Man, that was close!

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:19.520
Looks like we're gonna manage to get away.

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:22.870
Okay, we'll head left!

00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:24.540
Tetsunosuke, you go right!

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:25.980
Got it!

00:15:26.410 --> 00:15:27.690
See ya!

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:31.540
You're real evil, Shinpachi.

00:15:31.540 --> 00:15:34.700
If Tetsunosuke goes that way
with the collection of haiku,

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:36.200
Mr. Hijikata won't be...

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:43.040
You really shouldn't...

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:47.590
be so wasteful of these nice vegetables.

00:15:47.870 --> 00:15:50.050
Don't you agree?

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:53.890
Mommy!

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:55.910
You want to hear it?

00:15:55.910 --> 00:16:00.620
You want to hear a haiku of mine
after I've eaten a cucumber?

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:02.910
Do you?

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:14.660
Shinsengumi

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:14.660
I...

00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:18.200
I can't go on...

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:21.160
You've managed wonderfully, Tetsu.

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:23.040
Mr. Okita...

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:25.000
You must be tired.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:29.460
You did a fine job guarding the
collection of haiku from Mr. Hijikata.

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:31.800
Really, thank you.

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:33.550
Mr. Okita...

00:16:33.910 --> 00:16:34.810
Tetsu...

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:37.680
<i>Mr. Okita...</i>

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:38.880
<i>Tetsu...</i>

00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:41.160
<i>Mr. Okita...</i>

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:42.910
<i>Tetsu...</i>

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:45.910
<i>Mr. Okita!</i>

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:47.400
<i>Tetsu...</i>

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:51.620
Please forgive us...

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:56.700
We ran around the Mibu village 24 times...

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:59.410
Mr. Nagakura! Mr. Harada! Are you all...?

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:02.450
Ichimura!

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:04.120
Oh, I've changed my mind.

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:06.570
Tetsu, please hold on to this
for just a while longer, okay?

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:09.450
See you!

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:15.050
That's just cruel...

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:20.560
Give it back!

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:30.020
Hijikata...

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:35.240
Tatsu!

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:37.160
Tetsu?

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:40.730
Please, take this...

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:42.660
What's this?

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:45.580
Give it back!

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:50.000
Give that back!

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:53.450
Take it and run!

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:56.620
My secret treasure!

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:59.550
Mr. Okita asked me to!

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:04.220
Give it back to me! Give it back!

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:03.580
I'm begging you!

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:11.310
Here you are.

00:18:11.620 --> 00:18:13.800
Mr. Hijikata, please regain your composure.

00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:17.400
Thanks.

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:25.200
Hey, Tatsu! You're gonna betray
not just me, but Mr. Okita too?!

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:27.210
And what about you?

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:28.120
Uh-oh.

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:30.840
Is it okay for you to betray your own master?!

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:31.960
I'm sorry!

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:35.040
They have an odd shape to them.

00:18:39.160 --> 00:18:40.180
What do you think of it?

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:44.560
The taste of the Nagakura secret
recipe for stewed vegetables!

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:45.810
Hey, hand me the soy sauce.

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:48.200
It tastes all right,

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:52.540
but the shapes of the vegetables
are all lopsided somehow.

00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:54.700
It's not like I could help it.

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:58.120
Mr. Hijikata stomped all over them!

00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:01.790
I guess I'd have to say it's not
up there with Ayu's cooking.

00:19:01.790 --> 00:19:03.620
Argh! What did you say, Sano?!

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:06.250
I want seconds!

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:08.750
I'm happy that you understand this taste!

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:12.450
Forget the taste. I had a rough
day of playing tag, remember?

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:14.750
I'm just starving.

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:18.750
Forget the taste?!

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:24.370
Is this the mouth that said that?! Well, is it?!

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:24.370
Owowowowow, that hurts!

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:28.770
What's the matter, Tatsunosuke?

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:28.770
You think you can just say anything

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:29.910
about the stewed vegetables

00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:32.870
Thank you very much.

00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:32.870
Made by the Second Unit Captain himself?!

00:19:32.870 --> 00:19:35.620
Just to get Tetsu cheered up again,
Hey, that hurts! Quit it!

00:19:35.620 --> 00:19:39.870
You went to such lengths to arrange
that game of tag, didn't you?

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:41.290
I'm not gonna take that lying down!

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:42.660
But that certainly was unexpected.

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:44.790
What was?

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:48.660
I can't believe that even
Mr. Hijikata got in on it for him.

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:50.700
Forgive me for saying so,

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:53.040
but I guess he's actually the type
to throw himself into these things.

00:19:53.450 --> 00:19:54.790
You're wrong there.

00:19:55.950 --> 00:19:58.120
That was all in earnest.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:04.250
I said I'm sorry! Come on, I'm apologizing!

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:04.250
Take that and that and that!

00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:06.450
Gimme seconds! Please!

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:09.870
I've got no seconds for the likes of you!

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:12.830
I can't wait to have Ayu's cooking again.

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:12.830
How do you like that?!

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:14.400
You said it.

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:14.400
Seconds!

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:17.000
You guys are making a racket!

00:20:20.450 --> 00:20:25.210
"The precious snow has melted away
completely in the spring garden."

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:28.370
Is something the matter?

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:30.540
What?! Why're you joining in now?!

00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:31.550
If there were snow that

00:20:31.550 --> 00:20:33.830
wouldn't melt and remained pristine,

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:35.560
that would be something
to see, wouldn't it?

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:42.130
What's the matter, Toshi?

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:46.160
Soji...

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:52.560
Damn it, pulled a fast one on me, did you?!

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:55.770
Soji, you won't get away with it.

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:03.860
It can't be...

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:05.870
I will not say it a second time.

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:08.620
But...

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:11.620
He is a tainted being.

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:14.720
He is not a worthy friend for you.

00:21:20.290 --> 00:21:21.750
Master...

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:28.200
Suzu, you said you would be
my right hand, did you not?

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:29.910
Yes.

00:21:29.910 --> 00:21:33.500
Then prove it to me.

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:37.750
Take your brother's memento, his sword,

00:21:37.750 --> 00:21:41.770
and let it drink its fill
of a tainted one's blood.

00:22:03.620 --> 00:22:07.910
<i>Gripping the microphone tight,
the hit parade's on parade</i>

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:11.470
<i>Hey, Jimmy, how you feeling?</i>

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:15.790
<i>Quite the gentleman when he's off stage</i>

00:22:15.790 --> 00:22:19.480
<i>Hey, Jimmy, a generous spirit too!</i>

00:22:19.480 --> 00:22:23.400
<i>Being such an honest guy,
even his life's plain</i>

00:22:23.400 --> 00:22:27.290
<i>Keep building it up patiently</i>

00:22:27.290 --> 00:22:31.290
<i>May your dreams come true honestly</i>

00:22:31.290 --> 00:22:35.120
<i>Let's go for it again today, Jimmy</i>

00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:40.660
<i>You got to fight for your money!
How you feeling, Jimmy?</i>

00:22:40.660 --> 00:22:44.590
<i>You got to fight for your dream,
it's all too much</i>

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:48.500
